# Build context exclusions.
#
# This file has to live at the repository root, not next to a Dockerfile: Docker
# reads `.dockerignore` from the *context* directory, and both images here are
# built with the repo root as context because they need the root manifests and
# the shared package. An ignore file sitting in `apps/api/` is silently never
# read, which is how a 700MB node_modules tree ends up being uploaded to the
# daemon on every build.
#
# The `**/` prefixes matter for the same reason patterns are easy to get wrong:
# a bare `node_modules` matches only the one at the root, leaving every
# workspace's copy in the context.

**/node_modules
**/dist
**/dist-seed
**/build
**/.turbo
**/*.tsbuildinfo

.git
.github
.vscode
.idea
.claude

# Never bake real credentials into an image layer. `.env.example` is kept — it
# is documentation, and it carries no secrets.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

**/coverage
**/*.log
**/npm-debug.log*
**/.DS_Store
**/Thumbs.db

# Documentation and deployment descriptors are not inputs to either build.
*.md
!README.md
docker-compose.yml
render.yaml
railway.json
vercel.json
**/vercel.json
